## Reproducing the public measurements

```bash
npx vitest run tests/testing                  # replay machinery
npm run replay                                # oracle replay over committed fixtures
node reference-harness/runner/run.mjs --adapter reference-harness/adapters/ts/adapter.json \
     --fixture reference-harness/fixtures/synthetic-v1 --out <resultsDir>
node reference-harness/runner/grade.mjs --fixture reference-harness/fixtures/synthetic-v1 \
     --actual <resultsDir> --candidate-commit <full commit hash>
node reference-harness/browser/run-all.mjs --out <out> --reference-target vm
```

The corpus replay needs the private corpus and is a proof run, not a
development loop; the reference-harness grade needs only Node and the engine,
plus a Git checkout of the exact commit named by `--candidate-commit`: without
a qualified source the grader prints `NOT A GRADE` and reports no pass rate.
The browser journey run needs a Chromium browser and the Ruby reference
reachable through the SSH settings `reference-harness/browser/run-all.mjs`
documents; leave every `DECKO_STRICT_PARITY_*` switch unset to reproduce the
default-mode run. The skipped probes print what to set to run them.
